WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.467 --> 00:00:03.200
-It is so great to see you.
You look fantastic.

00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:04.334
-Thank you.
-"SNL" is back.

00:00:04.334 --> 00:00:05.634
This is my favorite time
of year.

00:00:05.634 --> 00:00:07.334
The first "Saturday Night Live"
this Saturday.

00:00:07.334 --> 00:00:09.234
-Yeah. We're back.
-Are you ready?

00:00:09.234 --> 00:00:10.801
Are you excited?
-I am ready.

00:00:10.801 --> 00:00:12.634
I'm very excited.
Miles is amazing.

00:00:12.634 --> 00:00:14.100
-He is good, right?
-Yeah.

00:00:14.100 --> 00:00:16.434
-Yeah, it's going to be fun.
I -- I want to --

00:00:16.434 --> 00:00:17.868
I told you backstage already

00:00:17.868 --> 00:00:19.901
some of my favorite bits
that you do.

00:00:19.901 --> 00:00:23.601
But doing your impression
of Anna Delvey on the show.

00:00:23.601 --> 00:00:26.133
-[as Delvey] Very V.I.P.

00:00:26.133 --> 00:00:27.367
-[as Delvey] Yeah, very V.I.P.

00:00:27.367 --> 00:00:29.701
-[as Delvey] Very V.I.P.
Very exclusive.

00:00:29.701 --> 00:00:32.300
-Now, did you start
doing it on the show?

00:00:32.300 --> 00:00:35.100
Like -- Just, like, on "SNL"?
-On "SNL"?

00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:38.834
-No. I've been obsessed with
that woman for five years.

00:00:38.834 --> 00:00:40.534
-Yeah.
-There was a Cut article

00:00:40.534 --> 00:00:43.267
that came out, and this was
pre-me being on "SNL,"

00:00:43.267 --> 00:00:46.100
so I would make videos
on the Gram,

00:00:46.100 --> 00:00:48.067
you know, front-facing.
-Yeah, of course.

00:00:48.067 --> 00:00:51.834
-And I got a wig and read the
article and then went to...

00:00:51.834 --> 00:00:54.801
[as Delvey] 11 Howard,
where she did her crimes

00:00:54.801 --> 00:00:56.734
by not paying for the hotel.

00:00:56.734 --> 00:00:59.000
[Normal voice] And I was like --
There's video --

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:01.734
I, like, have sunglasses and
I got kicked out of the hotel.

00:01:01.734 --> 00:01:03.501
-In real life?
-In real life.

00:01:03.501 --> 00:01:05.767
And then I went into banks
trying to make content.

00:01:05.767 --> 00:01:09.467
You know, like, "Run it again!"
And...

00:01:09.467 --> 00:01:10.901
-You were doing that?
-It was so cool.

00:01:10.901 --> 00:01:13.467
Yeah, 100%.
So cool to do it on the show.

00:01:13.467 --> 00:01:15.634
-But then this is fun.
So, you do it on the show,

00:01:15.634 --> 00:01:17.801
and then she reached out to you
about the impression?

00:01:17.801 --> 00:01:20.567
-Yes. She -- Well, yes.

00:01:20.567 --> 00:01:22.200
First, she invited me to her...

00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:25.033
[as Delvey] Anna Delvey
Foundation exclusive.

00:01:25.033 --> 00:01:28.467
Literally, it was, like,
very V.I.P., exclusive art show.

00:01:28.467 --> 00:01:29.868
-Very V.I.P.
-Very V.I.P.

00:01:29.868 --> 00:01:31.567
[Normal voice]
And I couldn't go.

00:01:31.567 --> 00:01:33.367
But then I realized

00:01:33.367 --> 00:01:38.968
that she had done a drawing --
in jail? -- of the "SNL" sketch.

00:01:38.968 --> 00:01:41.501
-She did a drawing of you
in the sketch.

00:01:41.501 --> 00:01:43.634
-In the sketch. In ICE, I guess?

00:01:43.634 --> 00:01:45.200
ICE. She's in ICE.
-Yeah.

00:01:45.200 --> 00:01:47.701
-I should get that right.
She's not in jail.

00:01:47.701 --> 00:01:50.734
Yeah, so she did the drawing,
and then I had to have it.

00:01:50.734 --> 00:01:53.334
And I was consulting friends,
and they were like,

00:01:53.334 --> 00:01:55.367
"Don't buy it.
Don't give her your address."

00:01:55.367 --> 00:01:58.767
And so I gave her my address
and my Social Security number.

00:01:58.767 --> 00:02:02.400
And $250 later...

00:02:02.400 --> 00:02:04.434
-You actually have
a piece of art from her.

00:02:04.434 --> 00:02:05.634
-Ay-ohh!

00:02:05.634 --> 00:02:07.067
-And you brought it here
tonight.

00:02:07.067 --> 00:02:08.968
-Yes. Look at that, guys.
-I actually --

00:02:08.968 --> 00:02:10.534
-I mean...
-I actually love it.

00:02:10.534 --> 00:02:12.567
-Yeah.
-And look. "SNL" up there.

00:02:12.567 --> 00:02:15.067
-[as Delvey] "SNL.
Run it -- Run it on my card.

00:02:15.067 --> 00:02:16.234
Run it again!"

00:02:16.234 --> 00:02:18.200
-I mean, come on.
-Yeah.

00:02:18.200 --> 00:02:19.734
-Isn't that wild?
-Yes.

00:02:19.734 --> 00:02:21.501
-By the way, can I look
at your -- at your nail?

00:02:21.501 --> 00:02:24.300
-Oh, yes.
This is "very exclusive for...

00:02:24.300 --> 00:02:26.234
-Can we zoom in on this? I don't
know what camera can zoom.

00:02:26.234 --> 00:02:27.868
--...for Jimmy Fallon."

00:02:27.868 --> 00:02:30.467
-Isn't that wild?
-"Nail art."

00:02:30.467 --> 00:02:31.934
-How did you get that?

00:02:31.934 --> 00:02:33.801
That "Tonight Show with
Jimmy Fallon" nail art?

00:02:33.801 --> 00:02:35.100
-You know, my friend did it.

00:02:35.100 --> 00:02:37.267
Yeah, she does --
she does little nail art.

00:02:37.267 --> 00:02:38.467
"So I don't look poor."

00:02:38.467 --> 00:02:39.767
[Normal voice]
I have to stop doing that.

00:02:39.767 --> 00:02:41.000
-No, that's alright. Yeah.

00:02:41.000 --> 00:02:43.200
You're always
very fashion-forward, and I know

00:02:43.200 --> 00:02:45.234
you're getting invited
to all these fashion shows.

00:02:45.234 --> 00:02:46.834
And you look great in these.
-Thank you.

00:02:46.834 --> 00:02:48.634
-Do you like
going to fashion shows?

00:02:48.634 --> 00:02:50.534
-I love it, I love it.
I love it. I do.

00:02:50.534 --> 00:02:51.767
-You really do?
-I do.

00:02:51.767 --> 00:02:54.167
I -- It's stressful,
I didn't realize.

00:02:54.167 --> 00:02:57.434
Like, well, first of all,
I'm wearing Tom Ford.

00:02:57.434 --> 00:02:58.534
-Hey!
-Yeah, hey.

00:02:58.534 --> 00:03:00.200
-That's what I'm talking about.
-Yeah.

00:03:00.200 --> 00:03:03.767
And this summer I
was invited to "Vogue."

00:03:03.767 --> 00:03:06.634
-Chloe, come on...
-Yeah. "Vogue."

00:03:06.634 --> 00:03:10.100
And I didn't realize
you have to be on time for that.

00:03:10.100 --> 00:03:11.868
[ Laughter ]
-What are you talking about?

00:03:11.868 --> 00:03:13.868
-Well, I -- like --
First of all,

00:03:13.868 --> 00:03:16.000
a fashion show
is about five minutes

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:17.934
because they just walk in
the clothes and then it's done.

00:03:17.934 --> 00:03:19.968
It's not like a play.
-Yeah, if it's five minutes.

00:03:19.968 --> 00:03:21.200
-If it's five minutes.
-Yeah.

00:03:21.200 --> 00:03:23.000
-You've been --
You know. You know.

00:03:23.000 --> 00:03:24.701
-Are you kidding me?
-Fashion god over here.

00:03:24.701 --> 00:03:26.133
-Please.

00:03:26.133 --> 00:03:28.133
-So, I thought it started
at 7:30,

00:03:28.133 --> 00:03:29.968
so I got there at 7:32.

00:03:29.968 --> 00:03:31.968
And everyone was seated,

00:03:31.968 --> 00:03:33.868
and it was, like,
me and Kanye West like...

00:03:33.868 --> 00:03:35.501
"Oh, sorry. Sorry..."

00:03:35.501 --> 00:03:36.968
-"Excuse me."
-Yes.

00:03:36.968 --> 00:03:39.400
And so I completely
freaked out about it.

00:03:39.400 --> 00:03:41.167
So, then I was invited
to "Tom Ford. Ver--"

00:03:41.167 --> 00:03:42.434
I need to stop.

00:03:42.434 --> 00:03:44.534
"Very exclusive, very V.I.P."
-Yeah, very V.I.P.

00:03:44.534 --> 00:03:47.367
-And I was panicked
about being late.

00:03:47.367 --> 00:03:52.133
And so I got to Tom Ford
an hour and 15 minutes early.

00:03:52.133 --> 00:03:54.300
And they were like, "Oh, well,
you're the only one here."

00:03:54.300 --> 00:03:55.934
-Because it's not
for an hour and a half.

00:03:55.934 --> 00:03:57.067
-Not for an hour and a half.

00:03:57.067 --> 00:03:58.634
And so I was like,
"Well, what do I do?"

00:03:58.634 --> 00:04:00.234
So I hid in the bathroom.
-Uh-huh.

00:04:00.234 --> 00:04:04.467
-And then ended up being, like,
the model for the photographer,

00:04:04.467 --> 00:04:05.834
like, to test their lighting.

00:04:05.834 --> 00:04:07.267
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:04:07.267 --> 00:04:08.801
-I think it was kind of good
because it turned out

00:04:08.801 --> 00:04:10.534
you got some good photos
from it.

00:04:10.534 --> 00:04:12.033
We got one.
Look at how good you look.

00:04:12.033 --> 00:04:14.434
-No one is there.
-There's no other human being

00:04:14.434 --> 00:04:15.801
besides you
at this fashion show.

00:04:15.801 --> 00:04:17.267
-Not a person is there. Yeah.

00:04:17.267 --> 00:04:20.267
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:20.267 --> 00:04:24.434
-"SNL" this Saturday.
Miles Teller, Kendrick Lamar.

00:04:24.434 --> 00:04:26.467
Miles Teller is a stud.
He was here last night.

00:04:26.467 --> 00:04:27.834
-"Stud"?
-Yeah.

00:04:27.834 --> 00:04:29.334
People went nuts for him.
-Yeah.

00:04:29.334 --> 00:04:33.200
And you said -- Yeah, you go,
"He does remind me of someone."

00:04:33.200 --> 00:04:36.667
-Yes. I --
run with me on this --

00:04:36.667 --> 00:04:39.567
think he looks a little bit like
my puppy.

00:04:39.567 --> 00:04:42.601
-Yeah.
And so your puppy's name is?

00:04:42.601 --> 00:04:44.367
-My dog is named Peach.

00:04:44.367 --> 00:04:46.901
A lot of people have said
he's hot for a dog.

00:04:46.901 --> 00:04:48.200
[ Laughter ]

00:04:48.200 --> 00:04:49.734
Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:04:49.734 --> 00:04:51.801
-This is him
when he was very young.

00:04:51.801 --> 00:04:54.868
But do you see, like --
You see a little bit of that?

00:04:54.868 --> 00:04:56.300
[ Laughter ]

00:04:56.300 --> 00:04:59.567
That eyebrows -- The eyebrows
are doing the same thing.

00:04:59.567 --> 00:05:01.000
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:01.000 --> 00:05:03.634
Yeah.
-[ Laughs ] That's pretty good.

00:05:03.634 --> 00:05:05.667
I -- I kind of see that.
But then --

00:05:05.667 --> 00:05:07.267
-Like, the mouth.
-Yeah.

00:05:07.267 --> 00:05:08.834
-The brows.
-You've got the brows.

00:05:08.834 --> 00:05:10.133
-Yeah, the cute little nose.

00:05:10.133 --> 00:05:12.334
-But -- But then you say
he also looks like Nick Jonas.

00:05:12.334 --> 00:05:14.667
-Yes, yes.
So, then he got older and --

00:05:14.667 --> 00:05:16.801
and, you know,
got into his hotter phase.

00:05:16.801 --> 00:05:18.767
Not that Nick Jonas
is hotter than Miles.

00:05:18.767 --> 00:05:20.767
Everyone's hot. My dog is hot.

00:05:20.767 --> 00:05:22.934
-We understand.
No one's hotter than anyone.

00:05:22.934 --> 00:05:24.701
-Okay, now -- Yes.
Look at this.

00:05:24.701 --> 00:05:26.400
-Here's your dog
looking like Nick Jonas.

00:05:26.400 --> 00:05:27.701
-Right?

00:05:27.701 --> 00:05:29.901
[ Laughter ]

00:05:29.901 --> 00:05:32.801
And, yeah, I got
a Hawaiian shirt for my dog.

00:05:32.801 --> 00:05:35.501
-Yeah, of course.
And then you said,

00:05:35.501 --> 00:05:37.901
"Well, I think I found out
who he exactly looks like."

00:05:37.901 --> 00:05:39.801
-Yeah, this was --
Alex Moffat was like,

00:05:39.801 --> 00:05:44.000
"Has anyone told you that Peach
looks a lot like Colin Farrell?"

00:05:44.000 --> 00:05:45.634
Wait for it.

00:05:45.634 --> 00:05:48.200
[ Drum roll ]

00:05:48.200 --> 00:05:49.501
-That's exactly it.

00:05:49.501 --> 00:05:52.300
That's who it is.
That's who he is.

00:05:52.300 --> 00:05:54.000
That's who it is right there.

00:05:54.000 --> 00:05:55.367
-Yeah, it's the brows.

00:05:55.367 --> 00:05:57.334
-Crush it this weekend.
We're rooting for you.

00:05:57.334 --> 00:05:58.734
-Thank you.
-And we love you.

00:05:58.734 --> 00:06:00.300
Thank you
for coming by the show.

00:06:00.300 --> 00:06:02.000
Chloe Fineman, everybody.
-Thanks, guys.

00:06:02.000 --> 00:06:04.100
-Catch the season premiere
of "Saturday Night Live"

00:06:04.100 --> 00:06:06.834
this weekend
with host Miles Teller,

00:06:06.834 --> 00:06:08.434
musical guest Kendrick Lamar.

00:06:08.434 --> 00:06:11.400
We'll be right back with a
performance from Arctic Monkeys.

00:06:11.400 --> 00:06:13.467
Stick around. Tom Ford!

